.TH tujoin n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tujoin
.PP
\fBtclutils::tujoin\fR joins two simple delimited text sources on a selected field. It is inspired by Unix \fBjoin\fR, but intentionally small.
.SS Load
.CS
package require tclutils::tujoin 0.2
.CE
.SS Examples
.CS
set left  "1;Ada\n2;Linus\n"
set right "1;Berlin\n2;Helsinki\n"

::tclutils::tujoin::texts $left $right -delimiter ";"
# -> 1;Ada;Berlin
# -> 2;Linus;Helsinki
.CE
.SS Options
.CS
-delimiter d     input field separator (default: tab); several characters
                 form one literal separator; must not be empty
-joiner j        output field separator (default: same as -delimiter)
-leftfield n     key field on the left, 1-based (default 1)
-rightfield n    key field on the right, 1-based (default 1)
-header bool     first line of both sides is a header line (default 0)
-outer mode      none (inner join, default), left, right, full
-anti mode       none (default), left, right, both
.CE
.PP
Field numbers are 1\-based. The joined result contains the key once, then the remaining left fields, then the remaining right fields.
.PP
\fB\-outer left|right|full\fR also keeps the unmatched rows of the named side(s); the missing side is padded with empty fields (as many as the widest row of that side has). The default \fB\-outer none\fR is the inner join.
.PP
\fB\-anti left|right|both\fR emits only the unmatched rows from the left, right, or both sides: the key plus that side's remaining fields, with no padding for the missing side. With \fB\-header 1\fR the header line is not emitted. \fB\-anti\fR cannot be combined with \fB\-outer\fR.
.PP
All options apply to \fBlines\fR, \fBtexts\fR and \fBfiles\fR alike, for example \fBlines\fR with \fB\-anti\fR and \fB\-joiner\fR:
.CS
::tclutils::tujoin::lines {1;Ada 3;Grace} {1;Berlin} \
    -delimiter ";" -anti left -joiner ,
# -> 3,Grace
.CE
.SS Errors
.CS
unknown option / missing value   TCLUTILS COMMON OPTION -name
-leftfield, -rightfield < 1      TCLUTILS COMMON INTEGER -name
-header not a boolean            TCLUTILS COMMON BOOLEAN -header
unknown -outer / -anti value     TCLUTILS COMMON VALUE -outer|-anti
-outer together with -anti       TCLUTILS TUJOIN COMBINE
empty -delimiter                 TCLUTILS COMMON DELIMITER
.CE
.SS "Additional exported commands"
.PP
Documented for completeness (same module, also covered by the test suite):
.CS
tujoin::files leftPath rightPath args          ;# relational join of two files on a key field (file variant of lines)
tujoin::lines leftLines rightLines args        ;# relational join of two line lists on a key field; all options above
.CE
.SS "Line ends"
.PP
\fBtexts\fR and \fBfiles\fR end the result with LF when one of the inputs ends with LF, and without LF otherwise. Versions before 0.2 never wrote the final LF. \fBlines\fR returns the lines without a final LF.
